   "transcript": "Interviewer: I’m in Milan, which many say is the fashion capital of the world. I’m walking down Via Monte Napoleone looking at the fashion houses shops. I want to find a typical lady of fashion. Here is a chic woman carrying lots of bags. Good morning, can I ask you a few questions?\nWoman: OK, but only a few.\n[Example]\nWoman: No, I’m American, but I’m living in Milan at the moment.\n[Question 1]\nWoman: I’m actually here for my husband’s job. He’s a footballer. He’s playing for an Italian team.\n[Question 2]\nWoman: No, he usually plays for an American team in Chicago.\n[Question 3]\nWoman: We normally live in Chicago, but we’re living in Milan for the moment and before you ask, yes, I love the Milan fashion scene.\n[Question 4]\nWoman: Yes, I’m working as a model for some Italian fashion houses.\nInterviewer: Are you enjoying that?\nWoman: There are few designers as good as the Italians – they’re fantastic.\n[Question 5]\nWoman: A bit, I miss a few of our friends there. I think the children are a little confused as we keep moving around.\n[Question 6]\nWoman: Yes, a little, not much, a few dresses, but it’s more like a hobby than a job.\nInterviewer: Well, you certainly look great. I have to tell all you listeners that this lovely blonde lady is wearing a tight-fitting simple red dress with very high-heeled shoes.\n[Question 7]\nWoman: Yes, of course – and you can buy it in this shop if you want.",
